: guile on the one part ( ἑτέρα ), matching itself against deeds of guile on the other ( ἑτέραις ), makes a recompense of woe, not of grace (as in return for good deeds): ἔχειν , epexeg. "(for the deceiver) to enjoy" (cp.
Il. 1.347 δῶκε δ’ ἄγειν
).

